nio: make the launchd exec marks use printf so they land in the core

Run 620 applied nio-mark-launchd-exec-steps.patch (status.txt patch 227),
but none of its three marks reached the kernel: nio_emark()'s string
constants are optimised away in this compile unit, while printf strings
(load_init_program: attempting to load) do land.  Replace the three marks
with printf so the next photograph can show which step stalls.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -7903,6 +7903,6 @@ load_init_program_at_path(proc_t p, user_addr_t scratch_addr, const char* path,
-	nio_emark("\nnio: LD pre-security-token");
+	printf("nio: LD pre-security-token\n");
 	set_security_token(p);
-	nio_emark("\nnio: LD post-security-token");
+	printf("nio: LD post-security-token\n");
 
-	nio_emark("\nnio: LD pre-execve");
+	printf("nio: LD pre-execve\n");
 	return execve(p, &init_exec_args, retval);
